Test Case 1 :

You are experimenting with a rectangular waveguide to analyze the relationship between its dimensions and wave propagation. The waveguide dimensions are a=4.0 cm, b=2.0 cmand the operating frequency is f=8 GHz.

Calculate the cutoff frequencies for TE10modes.
Predict the phase and group velocities for the TE10mode at the given frequency.
If the width of the waveguide is reduced to a=3.0 cm, how does it affect the cutoff frequency
and propagation characteristics?

AIM: To find the group velocity, phase velocity and phase constant of Electromagnetic waves in Rectangular Waveguides whose dimensions are a=4.0 cm, b=2.0 cmand the operating frequency is f=8 GHz.

CODE:
clc;
clear;
close;
// Rectangular waveguide - TE10 Mode
a_values = [4.0 3.0]10^-2;
b = 2.010^-2;
f = 810^9;
c = 310^8;
m = 1;
n = 0;
printf("RECTANGULAR WAVEGUIDE - TE10 MODE\n");
printf("Frequency = 8 GHz\n\n");
printf("a(cm)\tfc(GHz)\tVp(Mm/s)\tVg(Mm/s)\tBeta(rad/m)\n");
printf("----------------------------------------------------------\n");
for i = 1:2
a = a_values(i);
// Cutoff frequency
fc = (c/(2*%pi))sqrt((m%pi/a)^2+(n*%pi/b)^2);
// Calculate X
X = sqrt(1-(fc/f)^2);
// Phase velocity
A = c/X;
// Group velocity
B = cX;
// Phase constant
beta = (2%pif/c)X;
printf("%f\t%f\t%f\t%f\t%f\n", ...
a100,fc10^-9,A10^-6,B10^-6,beta);
end

