Test Case 2 :

In a radar system operating at f=15 GHz the waveguide dimensions are a = 2.5 and b = 1.25 cm

Compute the cutoff frequencies for TE10 modes.
Determine the phase and group velocities for the TE10 mode.
If dispersion is critical to radar signal accuracy, what strategies would you recommend
maintaining signal fidelity?
AIM: To find the group velocity, phase velocity and phase constant of Electromagnetic waves in Rectangular Waveguides whose dimensions are a= 2.5 cm, b=1.25 cmand the operating frequency is f=15 GHz.

CODE:

clc;
clear;
close;
// TE10 Mode
a = 2.510^-2;
b = 1.2510^-2;
f = 1510^9;
V = 310^8;
m = 1;
n = 0;
// Cutoff frequency
fc = (V/(2*%pi))sqrt((m%pi/a)^2+(n*%pi/b)^2);
disp("Cutoff frequency in GHz =");
disp(fc10^-9);
// Calculate X
X = sqrt(1-(fc/f)^2);
// Phase velocity
A = V/X;
disp("Phase velocity in Mm/sec =");
disp(A10^-6);
// Group velocity
B = VX;
disp("Group velocity in Mm/sec =");
disp(B10^-6);
// Phase constant
beta = (2*%pi*f/V)*X;
disp("Phase constant in rad/m =");
disp(beta);

